# SQA meeting with Tom about vibe coding QA

## global timeout threshold! (the suite, like gui tests, vst test)

- 5 min test time by default
    - break into smaller pieces if pieces need more time
    - if it times out, it times out, log it as such, move on (timeout threshold exceeded)
    - if as task terms: move to the next, notate but DO do the next text
- critical test failure
    - log it all and go back to the drawing board

## local timeout threshold (individual test tasks in a suite)

- 30 second time out
- should be a pass/fail most of the time
- build tests to try to rely on pass/fail, not "detailed" things

## try/wait

- for non-logging versions, get a screenshot when failed or timed out

## test scope

- one feature or task per test
- narrow scope
- FAIL FAST!
- some redundancy ok
    - (so that test 10 doesn't rely on test 5)
    - testing side paths are great!

## test structure

- cross dependent run sequentially, test files should never be cross dependent
- full tests can run in any order in the test suite
- give opportunity for chaos testing

## repo structure

- dev
- cert (qa area, release style code, no logging or whatever)
- prod

## test execution

- if you can, run multiple tests at once, but that might infringe on my allowances with subagents
- better to run a 30 minute test suite once, tan two 18 minute suites

## test scenarios

- low-redundancy, high-coverage
- maximum coverage, explicit bug fixes
- high confidence
- err on the side of coverage over redundancy
- time is fine, ai allowance isn't

## error reporting

- standard: high visibility with informative messaging
- automated tests are worthless without results
- headless should be pass/fail
- bigger tests should create detailed reports
- pull failures to the top of the report!
    - or, make a failure report and a full report
- screenshot all failures if possible, and if possible, pause execution to get a clean screenshot
    - test screenshots should be in it's own test folder, not the main screenshots folder
- stack traces should be logged, but I probably don't need to see them for now
- timeouts should be kinda granular and well-logged
- failures should be VERY granular and better-logged

## writing automation

- test early, test often
- publish the good, iterate to great
    - start small!
- fail fast
- write good comments
    - this is probably good for tests AND the application code
    - comment the code like someone else is gonna read it later
    - even if that future person is you and you forgot what you're doing
    - add now, remove later (if necessary)
- structure now saves stress later
    - mistakes and failures happen, give structure to deal with it
- always be ready to roll back a dependency update
    - should be a manual process type thing
- code has no ego
    - K.I.S.S. ethos
- time tests (steps and total) and keep a log for metrics (total duration, average duration, anything else that seems useful), especially for the deeper dive testing

## wait until screenshot code

```javascript
// force screenshot on timeout
type ByStrategy = 'xpath' | 'className' | 'css' | 'id' | 'linkText' | 'name' | 'partialLinkText';
const BY_MAP: Record<ByStrategy, (loc: string) => ReturnType<typeof By.xpath>> = {
  xpath:           loc => By.xpath(loc),
  className:       loc => By.className(loc),
  css:             loc => By.css(loc),
  id:              loc => By.id(loc),
  linkText:        loc => By.linkText(loc),
  name:            loc => By.name(loc),
  partialLinkText: loc => By.partialLinkText(loc),
};

async function waitFail(eleType: ByStrategy, loc: string) {
  const byFn = BY_MAP[eleType];
  if (!byFn) throw new Error(`Unknown selector strategy: ${eleType}`);
  const testTimeout = 30000;
  const locator = byFn(loc);
  try {
    await driver.wait(until.elementLocated(locator), testTimeout);
    return driver.findElement(locator);
  } catch (error) {
    await failScreen();
    throw error;
  }
};

// take screenshot on failure if one has not already been created within the last minute
async function failScreen() {
  const testName = expect.getState().currentTestName;
  const targetIndex = testName.indexOf('.');
  const testTag = testName.slice(targetIndex - 2, targetIndex);
  const timeStamp = newTimestamp();
  let failureScreenshot = `${nickName}-${testTag}-${env}_${timeStamp}.png`;
  let encodedString = await driver.takeScreenshot();
  let screenshotFiles = await fs.readdirSync('screenshots');
  let errorFiles = screenshotFiles.toString();
  if (errorFiles.length > 0 && errorFiles.includes(testTag) && errorFiles.includes(timeStamp.slice(0, -2))) {
    await sleep(500);
  } else {
    await fs.writeFileSync(`screenshots/${failureScreenshot}`, encodedString, 'base64');
    allure.attachmentPath(`${failureScreenshot}`, `screenshots/${failureScreenshot}`, {
      contentType: ContentType.PNG,
      fileExtension: 'png',
    })
  }
};
```
